      "produced_prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: a single transparent side-view skateboard sprite for a 16-bit pixel-art street game. Create ONE skateboard only, no rider. Strict side elevation with both visible wheels at exactly the same ground baseline, no isometric perspective. A teal/turquoise deck with upturned nose and tail, thin orange accent stripe, golden maple wood edge, charcoal/navy trucks and outlines, two clearly readable cream wheels with dark gray center bearings. Crisp chunky deliberate square pixels like a high-quality 1990s 16-bit game; restrained palette, clean tiny silhouette. Deck approximately three times wider than the entire sprite height. Centered in a wide landscape 3:1 transparent canvas, generous transparent padding around every edge, full board visible. No glossy 3D, no painterly shading, no rider, no legs, no text, no branding, no floor, no ground shadow, no haze or halo. Actual alpha transparency. The game will add its own thin warm-white outline. Keep the board's shape low and realistically skateboard-like, with the wheels mounted below the deck.\n",
